;; M4T §5.2 unfounded symmetric cycle: r(1,2) and r(2,1) support each other
;; recursively, so pure proof counting leaves both rec counts positive after
;; the direct input is retracted.  Precise deletion must over-delete the pair
;; and reseed neither.  Input arrives through the JIT overlay API.
;;
;; Hand-verified sidecar contents after r0(1,2) is fed and counted:
;;   r (1 2) -> (input 0, nonrec 1, rec 1)   copy rule + swap of r(2,1)
;;   r (2 1) -> (input 0, nonrec 0, rec 1)   swap of r(1,2) only

table (r0 int int)
table (r int int)

rule
(r0 X Y)
-->
(r X Y)

rule
(r X Y)
-->
(r Y X)
